<if>
  <condition type:"AND">
    <item>
      type        : CONFIG_CHECK
      description : "Check for MPLS"
      item        : "mpls ldp"
    </item>
  </condition>

  <then>
    <if>
      <condition type:"OR">
        <item>
          type        : CONFIG_CHECK
          description : "Check for OSPF"
          item        : "router ospf"
        </item>

        <item>
          type        : CONFIG_CHECK
          description : "Check for IS-IS"
          item        : "router isis"
        </item>
      </condition>

      <then>
        <item>
          type        : CONFIG_CHECK
          description : "1.62 CISC-RT-000600"
          info        : "The Cisco MPLS router must be configured to synchronize Interior Gateway Protocol (IGP) and LDP to minimize packet loss when an IGP adjacency is established prior to LDP peers completing label exchange.

GROUP ID: V-216698
RULE ID: SV-216698r531086

Packet loss can occur when an IGP adjacency is established and the router begins forwarding packets using the new adjacency before the LDP label exchange completes between the peers on that link. Packet loss can also occur if an LDP session closes and the router continues to forward traffic using the link associated with the LDP peer rather than an alternate pathway with a fully synchronized LDP session. The MPLS LDP-IGP Synchronization feature provides a means to synchronize LDP with OSPF or IS-IS to minimize MPLS packet loss. When an IGP adjacency is established on a link but LDP-IGP synchronization is not yet achieved or is lost, the IGP will advertise the max-metric on that link."
          solution    : "Configure the MPLS router to synchronize IGP and LDP, minimizing packet loss when an IGP adjacency is established prior to LDP peers completing label exchange.

OSPF Example:

R2(config)#router ospf 1
R2(config-router)#mpls ldp sync

IS-IS Example:

R5(config)#router isis
R5(config-router)#mpls ldp sync"
          reference   : "800-171|3.4.2,800-171r3|03.04.02a.,800-53|CM-6b.,800-53r5|CM-6b.,CAT|III,CCI|CCI-000366,CN-L3|8.1.10.6(d),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ITSG-33|CM-6b.,LEVEL|3M,NESA|T3.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-216698r531086_rule,STIG-ID|CISC-RT-000600,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-216698"
          see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/26261"
          context     : "router (ospf|isis)"
          item        : "mpls ldp sync"
        </item>
      </then>

      <else>
        <report type:"PASSED">
          description : "1.62 CISC-RT-000600"
          info        : "The Cisco MPLS router must be configured to synchronize Interior Gateway Protocol (IGP) and LDP to minimize packet loss when an IGP adjacency is established prior to LDP peers completing label exchange.

